Maya: Heads up — running into a weird dims/format issue in the sample app when using the batching helper for embeddings. JS SDK returns vectors length 1536 but model payload is 1024, parser throws and downstream reranker barfs.
Jordan: Which model and which SDK version? can you paste the request + raw response body?
Maya: Using `instruct-embed-small` on js-sdk v0.11.2. Minimal request looks like:
```js
const resp = await client.embeddings.create({
  model: 'instruct-embed-small',
  input: ['a', 'b', 'c'],
  batching: { helper: true }
});
console.log(resp.data[0].vector.length); // 1536 in my run
```
Raw response snippet from server (truncated):
```json
{"data":[{"vector":[...1024 numbers...]}],"meta":{"model_dims":1024}}
```
Jordan: Ok so server returns 1024 but JS SDK is padding or applying quantization transform locally. That sounds like a parity bug with the padding helper.
Samir: Yup — quick summary from infra: python SDK was updated to honor `meta.model_dims` and pads to requested batch width; JS SDK still returns the raw wire vector. We didn't add `vector_shape` to the response schema previously. Two orthogonal problems: (1) inconsistent SDK behavior on pad/trim, (2) response lacks explicit shape metadata so clients guess.
Olivia: I opened PR 784 to add `vector_shape` and a server-side `batch_pad` flag to responses/requests. Will try to merge to main and push a canary.
Paul: Another related issue: our auth/retry layer currently treats 401 token refresh as retriable and replays the whole payload. If client retries after a successful refresh we end up with duplicate vectors in our downstream store (non-idempotent). Seen this in customer repros.
Maya: Confirmed duplicates — saw identical vectors appear twice when our retry policy did a blind resend after 401. Also rerank endpoint response format changed recently: it returns `score` as float in one SDK and `float_score` in another; parser fails with KeyError.
Samir: Temporary workaround: set `embedding.batch_pad=true` on request and set client retry policy to idempotent for the embedding call. We'll push SDK shims: add `padVectors(arrays, targetDim)` in JS and mirror the python helper. Example workaround in JS:
```js
function padVectors(vectors, dim) {
  return vectors.map(v => {
    if (v.length === dim) return v;
    const out = new Array(dim).fill(0);
    out.splice(0, v.length, ...v);
    return out;
  });
}
const resp = await client.embeddings.create({model:'instruct-embed-small', input, batch_pad:true});
const vecs = padVectors(resp.data.map(d=>d.vector), 1024);
```
Samir: I'll take the python parity and add a compat layer so both SDKs expose `response.vector_shape` and `response.pad_to(dim)` helper.
Olivia: Deployed a canary with `vector_shape` in response header to our internal staging. DevexBot: v0.12.3-canary deployed to staging — includes `vector_shape` and conservative retry defaults.
DevexBot: NOTE: canary only — enable via `X-Canary: devex-vect-shape` header.
Jordan: I can pick up the JS SDK shim after lunch. Will add an option `padToModelDims: boolean` to embeddings client and default to false to avoid breaking.
Paul: I'll update onboarding docs and the sample-app README to mention "verify model dims" + show how to use `padToModelDims` and recommended retry config (idempotent for embeddings).
Maya: I'll attach a minimal repro gist to the ticket. For now the sample-app in `examples/sample-retrieval` should be updated to call `response.vector_shape` if present.
Olivia: Once PRs merge I'll coordinate a docs patch and send a note in #announcements.
Maya: Thanks all. This explains several customer bugs reported this week.
Jordan: quick question — rerank schema mismatch, where do we standardize field names? `score` vs `float_score`?
Samir: We'll add a single `score` numeric field and deprecate older keys with a 2-release window. Implement compatibility mapping in SDKs.
Paul: ping me when PRs are merged and I'll cut a small "onboarding friction" post for the docs site.
Maya: :thumbsup:
Olivia: Thanks!
Jordan: grabbing it now.
DevexBot: Rolling canary metrics look clean — no regressed latencies on staging (embedding pipeline).
